course: dictionary
lesson: 5140
title: Inward: towards the inside or hidden inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inward means going towards the inside or the centre. «The door opens inward» tells you the door swings into the room, not out of it. The clue is the direction: in, towards the middle.
explain: Inward can also describe feelings. «An inward smile» is a smile you keep to yourself, so nobody else sees it. If a character has an «inward sigh», something is felt inside but not said out loud.
explain: A good check is to swap in the opposite word. Outward means going towards the outside. If «outward» would make the sentence wrong, then inward is the right meaning.
fact: Inward means towards the inside or the centre.
fact: Inward can also mean inside your mind or feelings, and not shown to others.
fact: The opposite of inward is outward.
fact: Inward can also be spelled inwards, with the same meaning.
fact: «Curved strongly upward and inward» describes mammoth tusks bending towards the middle.
exercise: «The door opens inward.» What does inward mean? | Towards the inside | Towards the outside | *Towards the inside, into the room | Very loud
exercise: Ben gave an «inward smile» during the test. What does this suggest? | A big smile that everyone could see | *A smile he kept to himself, hidden inside his feelings | A smile made of stone | He was laughing out loud
exercise: Which word means the opposite of inward? | Downward | *Outward | Behind | Sideways
test: «Pot and pan handles should be turned inward so nobody can knock or grab them.» Where should the handles point? | Into the sink | Out over the edge where children reach | *Towards the middle, away from the edge | Upside down
test: «She gave a quiet, inward sigh.» What does inward suggest here? | She sighed very loudly | *She felt something but did not show it | She was fast asleep | She was blowing out a candle
exam: «The giant planets scattered small icy bodies inward and outward.» Which word means towards the centre? | Icy | Scattered | Outward | *Inward
